<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hubert Murray</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1861–1940</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sir Hubert Murray</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hubert Murray was an Australian lawyer who governed Papua as lieutenant-governor from 1908 until his death in 1940. His long administration was paternalistic, restricting land alienation and forced labour while limiting economic development. He became the dominant figure in the early history of the Australian-ruled territory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hubert-murray.jpg" alt="Hubert Murray" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Hubert Newman · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hubert_Murray_-_J._H._Newman_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
